[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'want weird proprietary software? You betcha. Drivers, accounts, apps, AI workflow enhancers. Like, I just want the words to go on the paper. Why is this hard? And it shouldn\'t be hard.'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Well, we\'ve been printing stuff since the \'70s. We figured it out. My microwave can heat up pizza without requiring an account, but printers just seem to be getting worse and worse. So, the last time I needed a new printer, I'

[01:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'decided I was done. No more ink. I bit the bullet and bought one of these things, an inkless printer. This one here is the PeriPage printer, and it wasn\'t cheap. I paid around 130 bucks'

[02:07] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Creator holding the PeriPage printer.
AUDIO: 'for this little guy like a year and a half ago, which is a lot of money for something whose entire job is paper go in, words come out. But, I took the chance and I am so glad I did. This thing has been a freaking champ in my'

[02:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'life. I even splurged on the fancy carrying case for it. I bought a giant stash of paper, and I printed everything I would have printed but with none of the headaches of a traditional printer. This thing is easy as heck, and I love it for that. And at this point, I'

[02:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'genuinely don\'t think I\'d ever go back to an ink printer, which brings me to my aunt. We were going to be heading to visit my aunt last week, and she mentioned that her printer was giving her problems. She said that maybe she'

[02:46] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: PeriPage printer printing a document.
AUDIO: 'would wanted me to take a look at it while I was there, and she was thinking about buying a new one. She doesn\'t need anything fancy, just documents, taxes, receipts, strongly worded letters to the mayor, you know, aunt stuff. And all the'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'printers she was looking at had the same problem: cheap printer, expensive ink, complicated software. Welcome aboard the misery train. So, before we went there, I I bought her an inkless printer. I just did it without asking. I just I'

[03:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'felt like it would solve her problems like it did mine. This PeriPage printer that I have isn\'t available on Amazon anymore, so I got her a different brand, which we\'ll talk about in a bit. I brought it over, and I set the whole thing up in about 2 minutes, loaded some'

[03:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'paper, and showed her how it worked, and she was blown away. The print quality was good, it was easy, it was fast, and most importantly, I got to tell her the magic words, "You never have to buy printer ink again." And just like that,'

