VISUAL: Creator holding a printed image of a warrior, demonstrating print quality.
AUDIO: 'Amazon that look pretty similar, too. So, I\'ll link to the Glorious Yang and a couple other decent-looking options in the thingy below. As for specs, I mean, it\'s a it\'s a printer. There there aren\'t many numbers to get excited about here. I guess the main thing is the'

[05:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'paper. It can handle US letter and legal along with A4, 4-in and 2-in thermal paper. And I\'m pretty sure the Glorious Yang can actually take different sizes, too. And you can use rolls or perforated flat sheets, whatever shape you prefer'

[05:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your dead trees. The print quality is around 200 DPI, which is solid for normal home printer stuff. And it has a 2600 milliamp hour battery, which lasts a super long time. I charge this thing so rarely that every time the battery'

[05:44] [scene:scene]
VISUAL: A man drinking from a can (cutaway).
AUDIO: 'finally dies, I\'m like, "Oh yeah, electricity. I forgot." And since it\'s wireless, you can just grab it and bring it wherever you need it. No power cable, no ink cartridges, no bag full of printer accoutrements, just printer and'

[05:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'paper. It couldn\'t be easier. These inkless printers use special paper, so you don\'t need to buy ink, but you do need to buy the paper because nothing in life is free, except like air, I guess, for now at least.'

[06:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Inkless printers are thermal printers. They use heat with a laser to burn the image into special thermal paper, which'

[06:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'has a coating that reacts to the heat and turns black. So, basically, it prints with science. There really only two major downsides. One, it only prints black and white, no color, not even any grayscale, just pure black and pure'

[06:36] [scene:result]
VISUAL: Creator holding another printed image, showing detail.
AUDIO: 'white. That\'s not a big deal for me because I almost never printed in color anyway, but if you if you want to print nice color photos of your family or your cat or Sonic the Hedgehog or whatever, this ain\'t your guy. And two, it only'

[06:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prints on one side of the paper. So, if you\'re a big double-sided printing enthusiast, well, first of all, congratulations on finding your thing, but you\'re not going to get that here. Now, you might think that buying special'

[07:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'paper is just as annoying as buying ink, but I don\'t think it is, mostly because ink dries up. If you don\'t use your printer for a while, it needs cleaning and calibrating and head aligning and whispering words of encouragement to it'

[07:13] [scene:result]
VISUAL: A printed character sheet for "ShadowDark" RPG.
AUDIO: 'just to get the ink to flow, if it even does. This printer just sits there. You can leave it on a shelf for ages, and when you need to print something, the printer is ready to go. If you\'ve ever needed to print one important document'

[07:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'only to discover that your printer has spent the last 6 months letting the ink go dry, and now you need to spend $30 on ink just to print one freaking document, you know how annoying that is. That just isn\'t a thing here. I should mention'

[07:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that the paper itself does feel different from normal paper. It\'s less rough and toothy and more like kind of smooth and silky. I actually really like the way it feels, but if you have a particular type of paper you like'

[07:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'printing on and and touching with your fingers and you like feeling it, then you can\'t use that here. There are two main kinds of paper that I use. The first is rolled paper, which is super convenient because the whole roll just'

[08:01] [scene:result]
VISUAL: A large, multi-page document printed and laid out.
AUDIO: 'lives right inside the printer. So, whenever you want to print something, you just turn it on, print, and tear it off like a giant receipt. Thank you for shopping at Tech Weep. Your total is crippling social anxiety. Please come again. The downside is that the paper'

[08:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'comes out with a bit of a curl to it. You can roll it backwards and flatten it out pretty easily, but it never gets truly perfectly flat. There\'s always a little bit of curl. I use this for unimportant stuff or stuff that will end up folding. Loading it is pretty darn'

[08:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'easy. Just open this up and drop the roll in and pull the end out the front and close it. That\'s it. It does come with these little spacers for the roll, but I never use them. I never need them for the letter size paper that I use.'

[08:40] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Various types of thermal paper (rolled and flat sheets) in a container.
AUDIO: 'The other option is folded paper and and that\'s my favorite. It\'s it\'s pretty great. It feeds through the back of the printer and because the sheets are connected, you can actually print multi-page documents this way. I usually just tear off what I need and print one'

[08:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'page at a time unless I have like a big long thing and then I\'ll just let it print and print. You just slide the paper into the back, it automatically grabs it from your fingers and it detects it and it lines everything up and it\'s ready to go. But, that\'s bit'

[09:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'basically the whole paper system. Rolls for maximizing laziness, folded sheets for when you want something a little more civilized. Both are great and neither one has ever asked me to replace the cyan cartridge before it\'ll let me'

[09:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'print something in black and white, which already makes this better than every printer I\'ve owned before it. The app is pretty basic, but it works really good. Connect your printer and boom, printer stuff. You can scan a document'

[09:29] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A smartphone screen showing the PeriPage app's document printing interface, listing PDF files.
AUDIO: 'right here from the app if you need to copy something or print photos from your phone if you got photos on there, you can print them. And there\'s even built-in tools and templates for making your own documents right here in the app. But, I have literally never touched'

[09:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'any of that. I bring PDFs, it prints PDFs. We have an understanding. It can print Word documents and Excel spreadsheets and PowerPoint points and all that stuff, but PDFs are what I use basically every time. Forms and then'

[09:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'documents and Amazon return labels, D&amp;D character sheets and adventures and monster stats, posters and plaques that I make for myself, and even my little mini zine games that I made a bunch of videos about. All those were printed on'

[10:08] [scene:result]
VISUAL: A printed character sheet on a desk.
AUDIO: 'this printer. So, I\'ve actually put this thing through a fair bit of nerdy nonsense. Getting a PDF into the app is super easy. You can do it however you want, but I just use Google Drive. On my PC, I toss whatever I want to print into'

[10:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a folder on the drive, and then on my phone, I open the file, hit the little dots, open with Paperang. I don\'t remember what the Gloryang app is called, but it\'s basically the same process. And then you get your preview'

[10:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and a few options. There\'s text or image mode. Text is for plain text, and it keeps everything super crisp. Image mode is what you want if there\'s pictures or graphics or big chunks of black, or basically anything more exciting than a'

[10:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'text form. And then you pick your paper type, rolled, folded, or perforated. I only use rolled and and folded. I I don\'t even know what the perforated paper is, to be honest. Then pick your paper size, and then there\'s'

[10:57] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: PeriPage printer printing text from a document.
AUDIO: 'concentration, which is basically how heavy the the print comes out. There\'s no ink, it\'s more just like how thick the blacks are. I almost always keep this on low. Everything is still nice and dark, but you retain more fine'

[11:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'detail, I found. And then, you hit print, and it prints. It\'s a pretty quick, about as fast as a normal home printer. And it makes this lovely little mechanical zappy noise while it goes. It sounds like there\'s a tiny robot inside'

[11:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'frantically drawing your document. Keep going, little guy. You\'re doing great. If you\'re printing multiple pages, it\'ll just keep feeding them through. And with rolled paper, when it\'s done, you just'

[11:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tear it off. And that\'s uh that\'s it. That that really is the whole process. I kind of don\'t know what else to tell you, to be honest. Like with a traditional printer, this would be the part where I explain cleaning the print heads and printing test patterns and'

[11:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'calibration, clearing jams, and installing drivers, fixing the Wi-Fi connection, and sacrificing a goat or whatever you got to do for these things. None of that applies here. There really isn\'t much more to explain. You just You'

[11:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'give it a document, it goes and now you have a document. That\'s all you\'re signing up for when you get a printer like this. And that\'s kind of why I love this thing. This video is'

[12:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'long overdue. I\'ve had this printer for ages. It\'s legitimately one of my favorite pieces of tech that I own, and I I kind of confused myself when I realized that I\'d never made a video about it. Like, I\'m TechTweep. I made this channel to share the stuff I love.'

[12:25] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: A gray carrying case for the printer with "Aproca" logo.
AUDIO: 'And I legitimately love this stupid little printer, and then I somehow just uh forgot to tell you about it. So, this video is me fixing that terrible mistake. I\'m here to show you a printer and tell you that it\'s good and I like'

[12:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it. I love how small it is. It just tucks away somewhere, and it waits until I need it. I love that the battery lasts for months and months. It charges with USB-C. It\'s wireless, and you can bring it anywhere. I personally do not bring it anywhere. I don\'t leave my house'

[12:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'often. Occasionally, I go visit my aunt, and once a year, I go outside to touch some grass just to make sure it\'s still there. But, I can imagine the portability being really useful for all sorts of impressive professional'

[13:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'workflows that I do not possess. For me, though, it\'s just my good old printer. I use it all the time, and it\'s never failed me. And it\'s one one of those pieces of tech that you kind of forget about in like a good way. It doesn\'t annoy me. It doesn\'t cause me stress. It'

[13:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'doesn\'t suddenly forget how Wi-Fi works or refuse to print because magenta\'s low. No account, no subscription, no driver from 2009 hiding in the bowels of Windows, no printer suddenly deciding that it\'s never met you before and you'

[13:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'got to set it all up from scratch and all that nonsense. This thing just sits there for days or weeks or months on end. And when I need something printed, it turns on and the battery is still charged up and it prints my thing. And'

[13:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that\'s it. No more, no less. And apparently that\'s enough to make it one of my favorite pieces of tech and I\'m sorry that I haven\'t shown it to you until now. Now, if you want this printer, well, I I don\'t have a link'

